          "title": "You'll want to know: எழுத்தாளர்",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "எழுத்தாளர் — eḻuttāḷar — \"a writer; an author\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "அவர் புகழ்பெற்ற தமிழ் எழுத்தாளர். avar pukaḻpeṟṟa tamiḻ eḻuttāḷar. He is a well-known Tamil writer."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural: எழுத்தாளர்கள், eḻuttāḷarkaḷ."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "எழுத்து \"writing\" + -ஆளர் \"one who …\". Compare எழுத்தர் (eḻuttar), a clerk."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "எழுத்தாளர் (eḻuttāḷar) is native Dravidian: எழுத்து (eḻuttu), \"writing\", from எழுது, \"to write\" (DEDR 853), with -ஆளர், \"one who does it\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
